<title>USA: Kaiser Aluminum to offer $175 mln of notes.</title>
<headline>Kaiser Aluminum to offer $175 mln of notes.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kaiser Aluminum &amp; Chemical Corp, a unit of Kaiser Aluminum Corp, said on Monday it proposes to offer $175 million in principal of senior notes due 2006.</p>
<p>The notes will not be registered under the Securities Act of 1933 and may not be offered or sold in the United States absent a registration or applicable exemption from registration requirements, Kaiser said.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to repay revolving credit debt and for general corporate purposes, Kaiser said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk  212-859-1610</p>
</text>
